From 0b4bac51a91e395d0c6c626ba6210f546ee99529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:43:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] webxr: add XRFrame.predictedDisplayTime

Expose when the device expects a frame to be displayed, behind
WebXRSpecParity. Inline sessions report the animation frame time, as
the spec requires, and so do immersive sessions on devices that do not
report a display time.

OpenXR already predicts the display time of every frame. Convert it to
base::TimeTicks with XR_KHR_convert_timespec_time on Linux and Android
and XR_KHR_win32_convert_performance_counter_time on Windows, and send
it with the frame data. Blink converts it to the page's clock.

Bug: 506004811
Change-Id: I62e6a34d2e5084da6a414306cf809d60a3606494
